		<section class="im-content im-content-flush im-content-lede" data-im-zoom style="--im-content-main: 100%">
			<p>A design system a Ghost theme can be <em>built on and sold with</em>. Not a starter, not a UI kit with a licence that stops at your own site: every line of it is original, every outside file is listed by name, and the licence lets you ship what you make.</p>

			<h2>What is in it</h2>
			<ul>
				<li><strong>107 tokens.</strong> Primitives with no meaning, semantic tokens that say what a value is for, and a bridge that hands them to Tailwind.</li>
				<li><strong>Forty components.</strong> Every one built from tokens only, with its knobs exposed as variables.</li>
				<li><strong>Fourteen collections.</strong> The page-shapes a site is actually made of — post, project, video, course, shop — each one a collection, a card and a page.</li>
				<li><strong>Five optional scripts</strong>, 1–3 KB each. Nothing is required to read a page.</li>
			</ul>

			<figure class="im-shot kg-card kg-width-wide">
				<img src="{{demo.six.[3].feature_image}}" alt="" loading="lazy">
				<figcaption><b>The docs</b> 84 pages, and every example renders the real partial.</figcaption>
			</figure>

			<h2>What it is not</h2>
			<p>It is not a theme you install. It is what a theme is <em>made of</em> — and if you want the theme as well, that is <a href="/collections/shop/">Signal</a>, which comes with it.</p>

			<h2>Questions people actually ask</h2>
			<div class="im-accordion kg-card kg-width-wide">
				<details><summary>Can I sell what I build with it?</summary><div>Yes. That is the whole reason it exists — the alternative was a paid theme whose licence made everything built on it unsellable.</div></details>
				<details><summary>Does it need Tailwind?</summary><div>It is written in Tailwind 4 and ships a compiled stylesheet. You can use the file and never run the build.</div></details>
				<details><summary>What happens when Ghost changes?</summary><div>Updates for a year. After that the version you have keeps working, because it is a stylesheet and some Handlebars partials — nothing phones home.</div></details>
				<details><summary>Refunds?</summary><div>Fourteen days, no argument, no form. Email me.</div></details>
			</div>
		</section>

